    "finalAnswer": "I fixed the bug in `truncate` in `src/lib/strings.js:16`. It cut the text to `max` characters and then added the ellipsis, so the result came out longer than `max`: `'abcde…'` is 6 characters when the limit was 5. It now leaves room for the ellipsis:\n\n```js\nreturn text.slice(0, max - ellipsis.length) + ellipsis;\n```\n\nAfter the change, `node --test` passes all 13 tests.\n\nOne edge case is still unhandled: if `max` is shorter than the ellipsis, the cut position goes negative and the result can be wrong. No test covers this, and fixing it would go beyond the smallest change.",
